Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:18:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] =?UTF-8?q?SystemUI:=20Bud=C3=ADk=20full=20screen=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?shade=20sheets=20that=20slide=20with=20the=20finger?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both Dual Shade overlays become opaque full screen sheets (iOS like) that
slide in from the top edge and follow the finger instead of the AOSP
container reveal. The reveal animated the size and alpha of the panel on
every frame (re-measure, re-record, offscreen alpha); the slide only moves
the sheet, which is a single offscreen layer while it moves. The bottom
edge is hard: rounded corners, a 0 x 3 dp solid edge and a grab handle, no
gradient or blur. The blur behind the bouncer is dropped as well.

The status icons and battery are shown once in the header; the clock and
date are shown once, large, in each sheet.
